150h|v|To soak, steep, or boil, in lye or suds; -- a process in bleaching. ; To wash (clothes) in lye or suds, or, in later usage, by beating them on stones in running water. ; To break up or pulverize, as ores. ; To copulate, as bucks and does. ; To spring with quick plunging leaps, descending with the fore legs rigid and the head held as low down as possible; -- said of a vicious horse or mule. ; To subject to a mode of punishment which consists in tying the wrists together, passing the arms over the bent knees, and putting a stick across the arms and in the angle formed by the knees. ; To throw by bucking. See Buck, v. i., 2.	o:1ufi,52,15;1ufb,46,54;1ugf,41,1;7v43,28,8;11gz,9,5~1ufb,46,54;1ufi,52,15;7v43,28,8;11gz,9,5;1ugf,41,1	s:1ynw,85,1;4rdf,73,1;606i,69,2;6zm2,30,1;8sle,26,1;2rxf,12,5;27ds,10,10~27ds,10,10;2rxf,12,5;606i,69,2;1ynw,85,1;4rdf,73,1;6zm2,30,1;8sle,26,1	D:1ufb,12,5;11gz,9,5~11gz,9,5;1ufb,12,5
