15c4|n|A sort of wild ox; a buffalo. ; A horn used by hunters. ; A copper instrument of the horn quality of tone, shorter and more conical that the trumpet, sometimes keyed; formerly much used in military bands, very rarely in the orchestra; now superseded by the cornet; -- called also the Kent bugle. ; An elongated glass bead, of various colors, though commonly black. ; A plant of the genus Ajuga of the Mint family, a native of the Old World.	a:23w7,78,9~23w7,78,9	n:23w7,47,1~23w7,47,1	N:ahyj,84,1;18dj,23,1;184m,20,4~184m,20,4;18dj,23,1;ahyj,84,1
