1672|n|A thicket, or place abounding in trees or shrubs; a wild forest. ; A shrub; esp., a shrub with branches rising from or near the root; a thick shrub or a cluster of shrubs. ; A shrub cut off, or a shrublike branch of a tree; as, bushes to support pea vines. ; A shrub or branch, properly, a branch of ivy (as sacred to Bacchus), hung out at vintners' doors, or as a tavern sign; hence, a tavern sign, and symbolically, the tavern itself. ; The tail, or brush, of a fox. ; A lining for a hole to make it smaller; a thimble or ring of metal or wood inserted in a plate or other part of machinery to receive the wear of a pivot or arbor. ; A piece of copper, screwed into a gun, through which the venthole is bored.	a:81ov,131,4;216i,124,13;1vfh,115,6;61dh,114,14;3fi1,113,2;9m84,111,55;4sg1,110,30;12ws,107,5;8n4,106,6;4058,97,2;59cn,96,9;84p3,93,8;7une,92,2;9geg,90,17;9m8o,85,5~1639,85,133;9m84,111,55;4sg1,110,30;48zr,69,22;43ai,9,17;9geg,90,17;6tr,71,15;ajfk,4,14;61dh,114,14;8s1h,1,13;216i,124,13;afhr,6,13;4xjs,68,9;59cn,96,9;84p3,93,8	v:4sg1,87,6;1639,81,102;8n4,80,1;3d0g,79,5;zxq,62,1;rpb,62,2;3c15,58,2;5sei,57,1;5pak,51,1;551e,51,1;84of,47,5;4xjs,46,2;4rkv,46,1;48zr,34,2;608j,15,1~1639,81,102;4sg1,87,6;84of,47,5;3d0g,79,5;27ny,8,3;48zr,34,2;rpb,62,2;4xjs,46,2;3c15,58,2;608j,15,1;zxq,62,1;5pak,51,1;4rkv,46,1;8n4,80,1;5sei,57,1	V:4lpr,90,18;45ap,88,1;7gy4,80,5;2wql,77,4;alpw,66,40;1ks1,62,4;4v6i,58,3;e4q,50,6;431g,49,5;3vpa,40,8;3kjt,38,4;3dbg,36,7;8oeu,34,16;ty7,33,13;trh,32,4~888b,17,50;alpw,66,40;5gzi,6,25;1883,5,25;4lpr,90,18;912w,14,17;9qf2,21,17;8oeu,34,16;5ego,23,15;ty7,33,13;6xl9,14,11;3l15,13,9;28co,19,9;5q2f,1,9;3vpa,40,8	n:3q4p,153,14;59b6,124,23;pul,115,5;4sg1,114,40;3sxs,112,5;1ypg,111,4;zxq,106,22;7day,106,5;9m8o,102,16;3mqj,100,395;3wz2,94,64;7riv,94,12;7dgc,90,270;1vfh,90,1;rpb,86,11~3mqj,100,395;afhr,50,279;7dgc,90,270;47w0,84,65;3wz2,94,64;a106,16,47;4sg1,114,40;8k2,79,36;afxf,85,35;59b6,124,23;zxq,106,22;1ks1,85,19;48zr,66,18;vn1,84,18;4xjs,77,17	N:8xo